  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Deep Blue Night will consistently trigger \"Unusual client behavior\" if a non-master player grabs onto the flying arrow at spawn.\nHow to reproduce:\n- Two VRChat accounts are required for this test. Desktop or VR does not matter\n- Have player A create an instance of Deep Blue Night ( https://vrchat.com/home/world/wrld_057ed75d-4915-455b-aee1-39a4f4e76ca3 ) and join it\n- Have player B join that instance of Deep Blue Night\n- When spawning, look 90 degrees to the left, you will see a \"Grab\" text, and approach it\n- As player A, grab the arrow and keep holding it until the journey ends. Player A (instance master) will succeed.\n- As player B, grab the arrow and try to keep holding it until the journey ends.\nObserved:\n- Player B will see a \"Unusual client behavior\" popup appear in the middle of the journey\nExpected:\n- The journey should succeed.\n- Worlds should not have the ability to trigger an \"Unusual client behavior\" error consistently.\nAdditional test:\n- Have player A create an instance of Deep Blue Night ( https://vrchat.com/home/world/wrld_057ed75d-4915-455b-aee1-39a4f4e76ca3 ) and join it\n- Have player B join that instance of Deep Blue Night\n- As player A, leave the instance.\n- As player A, rejoin the instance.\n- As player A, grab the arrow and try to keep holding it until the journey ends.\nObserved:\n- Player A will see a \"Unusual client behavior\" popup appear in the middle of the journey",
